WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.345
Welcome to ERD Studio.

2
00:00:02.395 --> 00:00:06.425
Let's turn your dbt project into a data model you can see.

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:10.145
Physical is what your dbt project builds.

4
00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:14.356
Logical is your design: the tables, keys, and how they connect.

5
00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:18.371
First, click 'Set up my AI helper' in the Welcome panel.

6
00:00:18.421 --> 00:00:22.824
It adds a setup guide for your AI assistant, and a small checking tool.

7
00:00:22.924 --> 00:00:26.382
No AI assistant yet? The panel links you to one.

8
00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:30.881
Then open your AI assistant in your project folder:

9
00:00:30.931 --> 00:00:35.382
Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Codex, Gemini CLI or Cursor.

10
00:00:35.432 --> 00:00:37.500
Type /erd-studio-setup.

11
00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.906
It explains every step as it goes.

12
00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:46.349
It starts by checking your dbt setup. dbt parse maps every model in your project.

13
00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:51.023
dbt docs generate adds the real column types from your warehouse.

14
00:00:51.723 --> 00:00:53.842
No dbt yet? That's fine.

15
00:00:53.892 --> 00:00:59.537
It reads your SQL and YAML files instead, and shows you how to install dbt later.

16
00:01:00.237 --> 00:01:03.174
Next, it suggests a business area to start with.

17
00:01:03.224 --> 00:01:07.679
That area becomes a domain: a focused diagram of related tables.

18
00:01:08.379 --> 00:01:12.413
Then it works out how your project is modelled, like medallion layers,

19
00:01:12.463 --> 00:01:15.580
Kimball or Data Vault, and shows you the evidence.

20
00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.754
Say yes, or describe it your way.

21
00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:20.271
It looks up the standard, plays it back to you,

22
00:01:20.321 --> 00:01:22.760
and applies it to the tables it writes.

23
00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:26.714
Then it writes your logical model: one file per table,

24
00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:31.545
with columns, types, keys and relationships from your dbt project.

25
00:01:32.245 --> 00:01:33.899
Now the important part.

26
00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:38.305
It compares logical with physical, just like the Diff button on the canvas.

27
00:01:38.355 --> 00:01:40.292
Anything that doesn't match gets fixed,

28
00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:43.290
and it checks again until there are no differences.

29
00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:48.365
Open a domain from the ERD Studio sidebar to see your diagram.

30
00:01:48.415 --> 00:01:52.001
Switch between logical and physical, and keep designing.

31
00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:55.706
No dbt project yet? Start with the sample,

32
00:01:55.756 --> 00:01:58.918
a small coffee-shop project that runs on your computer.

33
00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:02.419
Open it from the Welcome panel, the ERD Studio sidebar,

34
00:02:02.469 --> 00:02:06.595
or the Command Palette: 'ERD Studio: Try the Sample Project'.

35
00:02:06.645 --> 00:02:09.090
Pick any one, then choose where to save it.

36
00:02:11.301 --> 00:02:12.207
That's it.

37
00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:15.700
Rewatch this any time from the ERD Studio sidebar.

38
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.092
Happy modelling!
